WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.840
1801.

2
00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:06.420
A traveller rides through the
wind to a lonely stone farmhouse.

3
00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:10.820
That night, he writes warmly in
his diary about his new landlord.

4
00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:14.280
But look at what he
describes: a man at the gate,

5
00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:19.260
fingers hidden in his waistcoat,
eyes drawn back under his brows.

6
00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:22.950
Diary or picture: which do you believe?

7
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.850
So who is telling this story,
and why should you trust them?

8
00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:30.060
In this mission, you'll meet
narrators inside a story,

9
00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:32.520
and narrators who stand outside it.

10
00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:35.280
You'll separate who speaks from who sees,

11
00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:38.080
and track the order a story is told in.

12
00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:41.790
And you'll ask what makes
a narrator unreliable.

13
00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:46.550
Your mission: decide how far you can
trust the person telling this story.
